      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2003 S. Karger AG, Basel",
        "AbstractText": "We evaluated the clinical outcome and the prognostic factors at 6-year follow-up of patients with acute coronary syndrome without critical coronary arterial narrowing. The mean follow-up was 73 +/- 19 months. Mortality rate was 13%, and 20 patients (12%) had major cardiac event, 8 patients (5%) had stroke and 10 patients (6%) underwent revascularization. Multivariate analysis matched for age and ejection factor showed that moderate disease (stenosis 40-59%) (OR = 2.713, p < 0.024) was an independent predictive factor of major cardiac event."
      },
